DG CISF Visits Eastern Sector HQ, Ranchi

Shri Praveer Ranjan, DG/CISF, accompanied by Smt. Binita Thakur, ADG/North, and senior officers, visited Eastern Sector HQrs, Ranchi, on 19.09.2026. He reviewed the Sector’s operational preparedness and implementation of the MMDR Act under the Zero Coal Leakage Policy, with emphasis on effective surveillance, intelligence-led action, prevention of illegal mining and pilferage and strengthened coordination with stakeholders.

DG/CISF also visited the Dog Training School (DTS), Ranchi, and reviewed the training standards, operational capabilities and deployment preparedness of CISF K9 teams, stressing continuous capability enhancement to meet emerging security challenges.

During the visit, senior officers of Coal India Limited formally handed over the security of CCL’s Magadh and Amrapali Projects to the #CISF in the presence of the DG/CISF. The induction of these vital coal projects into the CISF security framework will further strengthen the protection of critical coal infrastructure.

The visit reaffirmed CISF’s commitment towards operational preparedness, effective enforcement of the MMDR Act, intelligence-led security measures, inter-agency coordination and robust protection of the nation’s critical coal assets.

